body:
Closes #554.

## Summary

This adds explicit `monitor` and `alert` role icons without changing node semantics.

A node can remain technically `type: "backend"` while using a responsibility-specific corner icon. The type continues to own semantic kind, color, legend grouping, topology, and interaction behavior. The icon only clarifies the node's established responsibility.

## Changes

- Add renderer-owned `monitor` and `alert` symbols to the shared semantic sigil catalog.
- Add both values to `common.schema.json#/$defs/nodeIcon`.
- Regenerate the standalone validators from the repository generator.
- Add authoring guidance that selects role icons from established responsibility, never from label text alone.
- Add a focused monitoring and alerting Dataflow example where both role-specific nodes remain `type: "backend"`.
- Extend the existing five-renderer icon matrix across Architecture, Workflow, Sequence, Dataflow, and Lifecycle.
- Add a real-Chrome regression for light and dark rendering, SVG export, and PNG export.
- Rebuild the deterministic `archify.zip`.

## Behavioral contract

Preserved behavior:

- omitted `icon` keeps the existing type-based default;
- `icon: "none"` is unchanged;
- existing icon names are unchanged;
- unsupported icon names still fail validation;
- no automatic label-based inference;
- no new component types;
- no remote icon loading or arbitrary SVG input;
- no routing, geometry, color, legend, brand, or Viewer interaction changes.

## Export and browser coverage

The browser regression verifies that both role icons:

- render at a measurable corner-icon size;
- remain inside their node bounds;
- do not intersect the node label;
- retain visible strokes in both light and dark themes;
- survive standalone SVG export.

PNG coverage also verifies icon content, not only output dimensions. The test exports the normal PNG and a control PNG with the two role sigils hidden, then compares the corresponding icon regions and requires changed pixels for both `monitor` and `alert`.

## Validation

Final candidate:

`b3280c64a2609e350bce48b4c6eba5872ffac4ff`

Upstream CI:

https://github.com/tt-a1i/archify/actions/runs/36066645735

Passed on the exact final head:

- full test suite on Node 18, 20, 22, and 24;
- Windows path portability on Node 22 and 24;
- shared Chrome browser regression gate;
- dedicated `Monitoring and alert icons remain readable and export-safe` regression;
- real WebM export validation;
- deterministic ZIP freshness;
- package smoke on Ubuntu, Windows, and macOS;
- website typecheck, build, and browser continuity;
- published update manifest validation.

The PNG pixel assertion was added after review feedback and is included in the final successful upstream run.
